.TH MD_GET_CHANNEL_COUNT 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.3.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_get_channel_count \- count the currently tracked channels
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

size_t md_get_channel_count(const morsedec_decoder_t *decoder);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Count the currently tracked channels.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of tracked channels, or zero for a NULL decoder. This query
has no errno-based failure return.
.SH REMARKS
Use indices 0 through count-1 with md_get_channel(). An index is an
enumeration position, not a stable identity. Channels can be created,
reordered, merged or retired during processing. Serialize enumeration with
mutation of the handle. The result is bounded by config.max_channels.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0.
Version 0.3.0 uses the float API and shared-library ABI 2.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_get_channel (3),
.BR md_get_characters (3)
